From 71d1fd4a63a63aa50852a95d799a8e54b3de2088 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qualcomm-toolbox <169756160+qcom-toolbox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:32:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] umi: WPA2-PSK for the Wi-Fi station

wifid hands the PMK over (Apple80211 ASSOCIATE, key kind 6); 0202
refused anything but open networks. New bsd/dev/sweet_wlsec.c is the
supplicant's half of IEEE 802.11-2016 12.7 for PSK + CCMP: PBKDF2 for a
passphrase, PTK = PRF-384, EAPOL-Key descriptor version 2 (HMAC-SHA1
MIC, AES key unwrap of the key data), 4-way handshake messages 1-4 and
the group key handshake. Checked on the Mac against the IEEE 802.11
PBKDF2 and PRF vectors, RFC 2202 (HMAC-SHA1) and RFC 3394 (unwrap).

sweet_wlce.c (ath11k mac.c / wmi.c v6.12 as the model):
- only WPA2-PSK/CCMP APs (group and pairwise CCMP, AKM PSK, MFP not
  required); our RSN element goes into the association request and
  message 2;
- PEER_ASSOC with WMI_PEER_NEED_PTK_4_WAY instead of WMI_PEER_AUTH;
- after the handshake: VDEV_INSTALL_KEY 0x5009 (tag 0x60, AES_CCM,
  pairwise idx 0, then the GTK with its RSC) waiting for
  INSTALL_KEY_COMPLETE 0x5003, then PEER_AUTHORIZE;
- a new GTK from a group rekey is installed from the poll;
- leave resets the encrypt type and forgets the keys.
sweet_wldp.c: TCL encrypt type CCMP_128 (6) once the pairwise key is
in, OPEN (7) before and on open networks. sweet_wlsta.c: EAPOL frames
go to the handshake, not to the stack; a failed handshake after
message 1 is EAUTH (wifid: invalid password).

Also flame 0123's AppleKeyStore wrap/unwrap (from HackiOS) so securityd
can store wifid's network passwords in the keychain.
Association request: Privacy for a protected network and the AP's
short preamble in the capability field, as mac80211's
ieee80211_send_assoc copies them. An 802.11ax phone hotspot refused
WPA2 without Privacy with status 45 (INVALID_RSNE_CAPABILITIES) whatever
RSN capabilities, HT or WMM elements were tried; with it, accepted at
once. A refused association logs the reply's elements and the AP's RSN
element / element kinds; transmit completions are counted by release
source and reason (every 5 min while joined).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
